slopmop report   <folder>
[x] HIGH - 12 impacts: 8 high, 2 medium, 2 low
[x] high   [!] medium   [i] low

Impact
  [x] Privileged access obtained
      A principal was given a privileged role or permission, or a route to root on a host was opened. Treat what it governs as under attacker control until reviewed.
      basis    SudoersModification, SetuidBit, ContainerEscape
  [x] Credentials exposed
      Secrets, keys, certificates or stored passwords were read. Treat them as known to the attacker.
      exposed  hash of deploy: $6$fixturesalt$fixturehashvalue0123456789abcdef
               password of app_rw: Fixture-Pass-01
               token: fixture-token-0123456789
      basis    ShadowFileRead, PrivateKeyRead, CredentialFileRead, ShellHistoryRead, CloudMetadataAccess, ClusterSecretRead, exposed password
  [x] Persistence established
      A way back in was created: a credential, an account, a key, a scheduled job, a service or a start-up entry. Access survives a password reset.
      exposed  username: svc
      basis    ScheduledJobCreation, SystemdUnitCreation, AccountCreation, SshKeyPersistence, ShellProfilePersistence, Persistence tools
  [x] Data collected
      Mail, chat, documents or files were gathered in bulk. Treat their content as disclosed.
      basis    ArchiveCreation, Collection tools
  [x] Data may have left the environment
      A transfer out was run. Confirm what was sent and where.
      basis    FileUpload, Exfiltration tools
  [x] Outside hosts contacted
      Files or commands were fetched from, or a channel was opened to, hosts outside the environment. Affected: 198.51.100.7, 203.0.113.40, 203.0.113.41.
      basis    ShellDownloadAndExecute, ReverseShell
  [x] Movement to other systems
      Tools that reach other systems were run. Hosts beyond this one may be affected.
      exposed  username: ops
      basis    LateralMovement tools
  [x] Defences and logging impaired
      Logs were cleared or security tooling was interfered with. Records of this period are incomplete.
      basis    LogDeletion, HistoryDisabling, SecurityToolDisabling, FirewallDisabling, DefenseImpairment tools
  [!] Code run outside normal controls
      Code was run in ways that avoid application control and leave little on disk.
      basis    ShellDownloadAndExecute
  [!] Traces hidden
      Files or history were removed or disguised. What is left on the host is incomplete.
      basis    HistoryClearing, Timestomp
  [i] Commands generated by an AI agent
      The scripts were written by an AI agent, which is the premise of this tool. Generated commands differ from run to run, so a detection that matches exact text misses them.
      basis    the premise of the tool
  [i] Environment mapped
      Identities, resources or configuration were listed. Later steps were probably aimed with the result.
      exposed  username: app_rw
               username: daemon
               username: deploy
               username: root
               email: alerts@corp.example
      basis    SetuidFileSearch, ServiceDiscovery, RemoteSystemDiscovery, NetworkServiceDiscovery, LocalAccountEnumeration, Discovery tools, exposed username, exposed email, exposed device, exposed ip

Remediation   (most urgent first)
  [x] Revoke sessions and reset identities
      Revoke the sessions and tokens of every identity in the evidence and reset its credentials.
      exposed  username: ops
      basis    LateralMovement tools
  [x] Rotate what was read
      Rotate every secret, key and certificate that was read, and reset the accounts of any host whose credentials were dumped.
      exposed  hash of deploy: $6$fixturesalt$fixturehashvalue0123456789abcdef
               password of app_rw: Fixture-Pass-01
               token: fixture-token-0123456789
      basis    ShadowFileRead, PrivateKeyRead, CredentialFileRead, ShellHistoryRead, CloudMetadataAccess, ClusterSecretRead, exposed password
  [x] Remove persistence
      Delete the scheduled jobs, services, accounts, keys and start-up entries that were created, and the files they start.
      exposed  username: svc
      basis    ScheduledJobCreation, SystemdUnitCreation, AccountCreation, SshKeyPersistence, ShellProfilePersistence, Persistence tools
  [x] Undo privilege changes on hosts
      Put sudo rules, file modes and container settings back to their approved state, and treat the host as held at root until rebuilt.
      basis    SudoersModification, SetuidBit, ContainerEscape
  [x] Restore security tooling
      Turn the stopped security services, audit rules and firewall back on, and confirm that each reports again.
      basis    SecurityToolDisabling, FirewallDisabling
  [x] Block and hunt the infrastructure
      Block the addresses and domains in the findings, and search proxy, DNS and firewall logs for other hosts that reached them.
      basis    ShellDownloadAndExecute, FileUpload, ReverseShell
  [x] Scope the data taken
      Establish from audit logs which mailboxes, chats, sites and files were read or sent out, and assess that data as breached.
      basis    FileUpload, ArchiveCreation, Collection tools, Exfiltration tools
  [!] Find the delivered files
      Collect the files that were downloaded, dropped or loaded, hash them, and search every host for the same hashes.
      basis    ShellDownloadAndExecute
  [!] Recover the missing logs
      Treat local logs as incomplete, and recover the period from a central collector or a backup.
      basis    LogDeletion, HistoryClearing, HistoryDisabling, Timestomp, DefenseImpairment tools
  [i] Follow what was enumerated
      Use what was listed to predict targets: check those identities, vaults and hosts for later activity.
      exposed  username: app_rw
               username: daemon
               username: deploy
               username: root
               email: alerts@corp.example
      basis    SetuidFileSearch, ServiceDiscovery, RemoteSystemDiscovery, NetworkServiceDiscovery, LocalAccountEnumeration, Discovery tools, exposed username, exposed email, exposed device, exposed ip

